     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to **5,100 mg/day**. That is double the maximum labeled daily dose for adults, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum per dose of about 850 mg to 1,000 mg. At this dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially.\n\nYou may have meant one of these:\n- **850 mg three times daily with meals.** That is 2,550 mg/day, the maximum.\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, for example 850 mg twice daily.\n- **500 mg to 1,000 mg two or three times daily**, depending on the titration plan.\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me that and I can add a note with the rationale. I'd still suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
      }
     ],
